Z||000000||Hardworker||05-11-2001||12:27 AM||||Have an 88 Formula 5 spd with slight pinon whine.  Also have a Getrag 284 from a 91 Olds Supreme 3.4 TDC in the garage. Been thinking about swaping the 284 for the 282. It appears the VSS is different. The clutch slave and throwout bearing release arrangement is somewhat different.  Other than that what else may be a problem?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||05-11-2001||07:43 AM||||Check out Rodney Dickman's site.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <P>Click on the Transaxle tab.<P>He's got about as much Getrag info as anybody.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hardworker||05-11-2001||10:21 PM||||Talked to Rodney on the phone and he was puzzled about the exact transmission I had when I told him the shift rod the shift arms connect to was the same height as the Fiero getrag at 2.5 inches.  He indicated the FWD transmissions he is familiar with the shift rod is shorter.<BR>The slave cyl on this transmission is external and the throwout bearing fork pulls the throwout bearing instead of pushing to release the clutch.<BR>There is a little note attached permanently to the transmission warning not to disassemble consult all service bulletins and call 1 800 832 4446 for exchange info. The only reason I would split the case would be to install the VSS gear and then use the Fiero sine wave generator.  If there is a device that will convert the pulses from the pickup on the 284 and convert them to a square wave would appear to be a better solution .||||reg||1
